analysis:
This batch contains only test code and test fixtures.

ClusterRuntimeApprovalFactsTests.swift (head 375-901) covers:
- model-argument parsing and candidate listing;
- the ClusterPublicModels declaration of two models (GLM-5.3-flash and Qwen3.8-27B), pipeline and tensor-parallel families on two M5 Ultras;
- the evidence-document SHA-256 pin and parity qualifications;
- pair-serving grants, including diverged-record exclusion;
- release candidate selection, and refusal of mismatched catalog.json entries.

The Fixture (795-835) uses a shell worker stub in a temporary directory resolved with realpath. Test lines 575-580 assert that a declared model's grant is its declared families with the evidence digest "whatever the records say". That is a production policy: declaration overrides bundled parity records. Integration should confirm in ClusterRuntimeApprovalFacts and ClusterPublicModels sources, not in this batch, that:
- the declaration is build-baked and not provider- or consumer-controllable;
- the coordinator still independently gates approvals (TB-011, T-054, A-017).

Request-envelope limits of 1,048,576 prompt and output tokens (436) and media for tensor parallel only (441-444, 478-482) are asserted. Their enforcement lives in unseen production code.

The new fixture glm-5.3-flash-dev-branch17.json (line 1) is a static darkbloom_cluster_runtime_v2 facts document. It contains public digests only; no secrets were observed.

ClusterApprovalFixture.swift adds a Shape enum (head 32-38) and a qwen27 tensor-parallel capability (105-125). It also sets generationMode/tensorAssistant in saved setups (155-158). This is test scaffolding only.

No production source in this batch changes trust boundaries, so no regression was identified. Production changes to grant/declaration logic should be reviewed in other batches.
